      "id": "EHV-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-prv-component",
      "title": "A lowest weight added to a highest weight gives a component of the tensor product",
      "hypotheses": "V is finite-dimensional and irreducible under the compact operators, with a highest-weight vector of weight Λ. U is finite-dimensional with a positive form for which E_ab* = E_ba, f ∈ U is a nonzero lowest-weight vector of weight ν, and Λ + ν is dominant on each sign block.",
      "statement": "V ⊗ U contains a nonzero highest-weight vector of weight Λ + ν.",
      "definitions": [
        "The auxiliary module is the compact type of highest weight ⌊Λ + ν⌋ with each diagonal operator shifted by the fractional part of Λ + ν, which is constant on blocks."
      ],
